$ weave schedules --help
The Dispatcher's schedules, which start a headless turn on one of your Hosts, or prompt one of your Bots, at the times a cron expression gives or once: list, add, remove, pause, resume or run one, or see what they did

Usage: weave schedules [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list         The schedules, when each runs next and how it last went (the default)
  add          Add a schedule: at the times `--cron` gives, or once `--at` a time, start a headless turn on a Host, or prompt a Bot
  remove       Forget a schedule and what it did. A turn it started runs on
  pause        Run nothing on schedule until resumed
  resume       Run on schedule again from now, catching up nothing missed while paused
  run          Run it now, paused or not, as an occurrence of its own
  occurrences  What schedules did each time they came due, newest first
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave schedules list --help
The schedules, when each runs next and how it last went (the default)

Usage: weave schedules list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print them as JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave schedules add --help
Add a schedule: at the times `--cron` gives, or once `--at` a time, start a headless turn on a Host, or prompt a Bot

Usage: weave schedules add [OPTIONS] <--cron <CRON>|--at <TIME>> <NAME> [-- <PROMPT>...]

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          Its name, unique among the Dispatcher's schedules

  [PROMPT]...
          The prompt; read from stdin when omitted or `-`

Options:
      --cron <CRON>
          When it runs: five fields, minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week, such as "0 9 * * 1-5" for 09:00 on weekdays; or @hourly, @daily, @weekly, @monthly

      --at <TIME>
          Run once, at this time, in place of --cron: 2026-11-12 09:00, in --zone, or 2026-11-12T09:00:00+02:00

      --zone <ZONE>
          The IANA time zone its times are in, such as Africa/Johannesburg; the Dispatcher's computer's when omitted, or with --at, this computer's

      --bot <BOT>
          Prompt this Bot, by its name or id, in place of --host, --agent, --cwd and the rest: each time goes into its thread, or starts its first, as the Bot is set up then

      --host <HOST>
          The Host it runs on, by name or id: one `weave hosts` lists

      --agent <AGENT>
          The agent on that Host, as `weave agents` lists them there

      --cwd <CWD>
          The directory on that Host it runs in; `~/` starts at the home there. This directory when omitted

      --project <PROJECT>
          Run in a Project, by its name or id as `weave projects` lists them: in its location on that Host, a repository's primary worktree. A Project with no location there is refused

      --thread <THREAD>
          Prompt this thread each time, by its id, instead of starting a new one

      --mode <MODE>
          The mode a new thread starts in; the agent's configured one when omitted

      --approve <KINDS>
          Tool kinds to allow, comma-separated: read, edit, delete, move, search, execute, think, fetch, switch_mode, other; or all. Everything else is rejected

      --missed <MISSED>
          What to do about a time it missed, as while the Dispatcher's computer slept: run the latest once, late, within a week (the default), or skip it
          
          [default: latest]
          [possible values: latest, skip]

      --allow-overlap
          Start an occurrence while its previous one is still waiting or running, in a thread of its own; by default it's skipped

  -h, --help
          Print help

