$ weave projects --help
Your Projects, which the Dispatcher keeps, each with a location on one or more of your Hosts: list them, register a directory as one, rename one, or remove one

Usage: weave projects [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list    The Projects and where each is on your Hosts (the default). While the Dispatcher doesn't answer, the ones it listed last, saying how long ago
  add     Register a directory as a Project, or as its location on another Host: a repository by its primary worktree, so all its worktrees are in it, or a directory outside one
  show    A Project and where it is on your Hosts
  rename  Rename a Project
  update  Change a Project: remove its location on one Host
  remove  Forget a Project and all its locations. What's in its directories stays
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

