$ weave projects add --help
Register a directory as a Project, or as its location on another Host: a repository by its primary worktree, so all its worktrees are in it, or a directory outside one

Usage: weave projects add [OPTIONS] [DIR]

Arguments:
  [DIR]
          The directory; this one when omitted. With --host, one on that computer, given whole or under ~, and this one's counterpart under the home there when omitted

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          What to call a new Project; the directory's name, a repository's primary worktree's, when omitted

      --to <PROJECT>
          Add the directory to this Project, by its name or id, as its location on the Host, rather than making a new one

      --host <HOST>
          The Host the directory is on, by its id or name as `weave hosts` lists them, reached through the Dispatcher; this computer's when omitted

      --json
          Print the Project as JSON. It asks nothing: a clone of a repository a Project has on other Hosts needs --to or --name

  -h, --help
          Print help

