$ weave bots update --help
Change a Bot. A thread it has open keeps the approvals and mode it started with

Usage: weave bots update [OPTIONS] <BOT>

Arguments:
  <BOT>
          The Bot's name or id

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          Its new name

      --approve <KINDS>
          Tool kinds its threads approve without asking you, in place of those they do now, comma-separated: read, edit, delete, move, search, execute, think, fetch, switch_mode, other; or all. It asks you about the rest

      --no-approve
          Approve nothing: ask you about every tool

      --mode <MODE>
          The mode its threads start in

      --no-mode
          Start its threads in the agent's configured mode

      --new-thread-at <HH:MM>
          Start a new thread every day at this time, in its zone, once its thread has had a turn

      --no-new-thread-at
          Start a new thread only when asked

      --zone <ZONE>
          The IANA time zone its times are in, such as Africa/Johannesburg

      --pause-after <DURATION>
          How long a request in its thread may wait for you before its schedules pause: 90s, 30m, 12h

      --json
          Print the Bot as JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help

